From: quantforge-br <218010578+quantforge-br@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: gts3llte: enable the top speaker pair

The SM-T825 device tree reserved TLMM 58-61 and dropped the quaternary
TDM link because TrustZone might own those pins on the LTE model. The
stock gts3llte device trees (Rev00/02/04/05) show it does not: the eSE
SPI on those pins (spi@75b9000) is disabled, and the quaternary MI2S DAI
applies quat_mi2s_active (gpio58-61) as its default pinctrl state on
every boot, next to a quaternary TDM RX group (port 0x9030, 3.072 MHz)
for the top speakers.

Tested on an SM-T825: no reset with gpio58-61 claimed and read through
debugfs, both RT5508 pairs play (left channel on the top pair, right on
the bottom pair).
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-samsung-gts3llte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-samsung-gts3llte.dts
@@ -7,12 +7,15 @@
  * compatible.
  *
  * Not here yet: the modem (LTE, SIM, GPS) - only its shared memory region is
- * reserved. TLMM 58-61 stay reserved: stock comments out the eSE SPI on both
- * models and they are free on the Wi-Fi model, but which pins TrustZone owns
- * is set by its firmware and an owned pin resets the tablet about 9 s into
- * boot. So the top speaker pair (quaternary TDM on those pins) is left out
- * until it is checked on an SM-T825; the bottom pair, headphones and
- * microphones stay.
+ * reserved.
+ *
+ * TLMM 58-61 are not reserved here either, so the top speaker pair
+ * (quaternary TDM) works like on the Wi-Fi model. The stock gts3llte device
+ * trees (Rev00/02/04/05) keep the eSE SPI on those pins (spi@75b9000)
+ * disabled, and their quaternary MI2S DAI applies quat_mi2s_active
+ * (gpio58-61) as its default pinctrl state on every boot, next to a
+ * quaternary TDM RX group (port 0x9030, 3.072 MHz) for the top speakers:
+ * TrustZone does not own these pins on the SM-T825 either.
  */
 
 #include "apq8096-samsung-gts3lwifi.dts"
@@ -33,14 +36,3 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
-
-&tlmm {
-	/delete-property/ gpio-reserved-ranges;
-	gpio-reserved-ranges = <25 4>, <58 4>;
-};
-
-&sound {
-	pinctrl-0 = <&pri_tdm_clk_default>, <&pri_tdm_data_default>;
-
-	/delete-node/ spk-top-dai-link;
-};
